  "note": "Annual election of six urban councillors, nominations 5 January 1933; four candidates for six vacancies, so there was no contest (Irish News, 6 January 1933, p. 7). Retiring members were John K. Lyons, Leonard K. M'Gookin, William E. Milliken and John Hunter. The other two vacancies arose from the death of H. M'Cavana and the disqualification of Robert Clugston. Returned unopposed."
